        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================

   Most BBS systems allow 'file requests'.
   If you have a allfiles list of such a system, or the sysop posts his
   new files in echo mail .. you may want to have some of those files.
   You could login and download files, but there is a faster way,
   you freq the files with your mailer.
   You make a file request packet, send it with your mailer, and
   if the requests can be filled the files are send to you
   at the file transfer turnaround. This is especially handy
   if you want files from your boss, because you call him anyway
   with your mailer, so if you freq files from him you pay only
   for the seconds the file transfer of the freqed files last,
   because you have to make the connect anyway.

   So how do you make such a file request packet ?
   The simplest way is to use the 'freq' programm.
   You call it with the files you want, and ik makes a packet
   and adds it to a .flo file.

   Also you can use the Freq programm to get information on a
   node from the nodelist. This can be handy if you want to
   know the phone number .. or you want to check the location
   of the system before freqing from it. Or you just want to
   know if your freqing from the right system.


   How do you use this tool ?

   first you have to give the nodenumber you want to freq
   from on the command line. If you type return now you
   only get information about this node.

   for example 'Freq 14:103/300' gives:


Tron Freq Utilitie V0.76

NodeNumber :    14:103/300
BBS        :    Amiga Pet Shop BBS
Sysop      :    Paul Spijkerman
City       :    Gasselte Holland
Number     :    0599-564696


   If you want to freq files also you type them after the
   nodenumber .. like this:


   Freq  <NodeNumber> <File #1> .. [File #n]


   Some systems have files or a few files that need a password
   before it can be freqed, in that case you add a password
   to the file name in question by adding a ! and the password
   like this:


   File!Password

   For example:      Freq  14:103/300  tron!test allfiles.lha


   If you freq files they are shown in a list beneath the
   node information. A node don't has to be in a nodelist
   for the Freq programm to work. But after using the
   freq utility you have to call out, and for that there has
   to be an entry in a nodelist for that system.
   If you don't have an entry in a nodelist for that system,
   you could add it to the pointlist. That is a lot simpler
   than making a nodelist for that node because in the point
   list you only need to add one line.

   If you used the freq programm you have to call out, this can
   be down in the BBS GUI by typing F10, or from shell with
   the Trion or Caller utility.
   Look at the Trion and Caller doc for more information about this.

